@startuml Lens Lookup Sequence Diagram
title User Lens — pick a person, see their devices (de-elevated)

actor Operator as OP
participant "HomePresenter\n(coordinator)" as P
participant "PersonLensViewModel\n(detail pane)" as VM
participant "LensLookupWorker.ps1\n(pool, as admin)" as PW
participant "Scheduled Task\n(interactive user, Limited)" as TASK
participant "LensWorker.ps1\n(as the regular user)" as LW
participant "AD (Global Catalog)\n+ home domains" as AD
participant "SCCM AdminService\n(REST)" as SCCM

== Pick a user in the AD finder ==
OP -> P : click a USER row  (OnPickUser)
activate P
P -> VM : SetLoading(displayName)
P -> VM : HomeVm.SetPerson(vm)  -> DetailMode = 'Person'
note right of VM : detail pane switches to the Lens (loading)
P -> PW : BeginInvoke(Identity, SiteServer, SourceRoot)  on the runspace pool
deactivate P

== De-elevate to the logged-on user ==
activate PW
note right of PW
  DONUT runs elevated as the admin account, which cannot read SCCM/BitLocker.
  So the lookup must run as the interactive (regular) user.
end note
PW -> PW : find the interactive user (explorer owner)\n+ ACL a %ProgramData%\\DONUT exchange folder
PW -> TASK : register + start a one-shot task\n(LogonType Interactive = logged-on token, no password; RunLevel Limited)
activate TASK
TASK -> LW : run LensWorker.ps1 -Identity -SiteServer -ResultPath
deactivate TASK
activate LW

== Gather (as the regular user) ==
LW -> AD : GC-locate the user (forest-wide) -> bind home domain
AD --> LW : UPN / SAM / email / manager / office
LW -> SCCM : endswith(UniqueUserName,'<SAM>')  -> WSID(s)
SCCM --> LW : ResourceName(s)  (exact-tail filtered)
loop each WSID
  LW -> SCCM : model + last hardware-sync (by ResourceID)
  LW -> AD : GC-locate the computer -> msFVE-RecoveryInformation (BitLocker)
end
LW -> LW : write the JSON bundle to ResultPath
deactivate LW

== Return + render ==
PW -> PW : read result.json (poll)\nunregister the task + clean up
PW --> P : JSON bundle
deactivate PW
activate P
P -> P : PollLens: PersonLens.FromJson(json)
P -> VM : Apply(lens)  (person fields + LensDeviceViewModels)
P -> VM : wire each device's Reveal / Add command
deactivate P
VM -> OP : Lens shows info + devices (BitLocker hidden until Reveal)

== Act on a device ==
OP -> VM : click "Add" on a device
VM -> P : OnAddDeviceToList(wsid)
activate P
P -> P : EnsureRow + PrefetchIp + StartInventory + MoveRowToTop
P -> OP : machine added to the list (toast); Lens stays open
deactivate P
@enduml
